spi: dw: stream enhanced quad frames through DMA

The DesignWare enhanced transfer path requires quad writes to fit in
the TX FIFO. This prevents larger transfers from using DMA, while quad
reads also need their full instruction and address controls queued
before the first clock to avoid ending a frame prematurely.

Allow DMA-backed enhanced quad transfers beyond the FIFO capacity.
For TX, hold native chip select inactive while priming the FIFO with
the control words and a bounded payload prefix. Build a DMA tail
from the remaining bytes of the SPI core's mapped scatterlist, then
resume the frame after the descriptor is armed. For RX, preload all
enhanced control words before starting the receive clocks.

Preserve chip-select boundaries and SPI mode 3 idle-clock behavior.
Reject unsupported external chip-select paths, enhanced-write dummy
clocks and unsafe DMA widths or alignments rather than transmitting
an incomplete frame. Ordinary single-line SPI transfers retain
their existing execution path.

This change depends on the enhanced quad support in Raspberry Pi
Linux PR #7587 (81a76dd2284e09547cc5a9eeb88b174fea5a819a).

